---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Data Deletion Instructions"
  description="ScheduleRama instructions for requesting deletion of connected Facebook and Instagram social publishing data."
  activeSection="company"
>
  <style>
    .hero {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--navy-deep) 0%, #132543 100%);
      padding: 132px 56px 76px;
    }

    .hero-inner {
      max-width: 980px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 900;
      font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
      line-height: 0.95;
      color: #fff;
      max-width: 780px;
    }

    .hero p {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin-top: 20px;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65);
    }

    .legal-wrap {
      max-width: 980px;
      margin: -36px auto 72px;
      padding: 0 24px;
      position: relative;
      z-index: 2;
    }

    .legal-card {
      background: #fffaf2;
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 18px;
      box-shadow: 0 18px 48px rgba(15,28,48,0.08);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .legal-meta {
      padding: 28px 32px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.72);
    }

    .meta-item span {
      display: block;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }

    .meta-item strong {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .legal-body {
      padding: 36px 32px 44px;
    }

    .legal-body > p {
      color: var(--ink-mid);
      line-height: 1.8;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    .legal-body hr {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      margin: 28px 0;
    }

    .legal-body h2 {
      font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 900;
      font-size: 2rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      margin: 34px 0 14px;
    }

    .legal-body h3 {
      font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      margin: 24px 0 10px;
    }

    .legal-body ul, .legal-body ol {
      padding-left: 22px;
      margin: 14px 0 18px;
    }

    .legal-body li {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      color: var(--ink-mid);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .callout {
      background: var(--orange-pale);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--orange);
      padding: 16px 18px;
      border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
      margin: 18px 0 24px;
      color: var(--ink-mid);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .hero {
        padding: 112px 20px 60px;
      }

      .legal-wrap {
        padding: 0 12px;
        margin-top: -28px;
      }

      .legal-meta {
        padding: 22px 20px;
      }

      .legal-body {
        padding: 28px 20px 34px;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1>Social Publishing Data Deletion</h1>
      <p>This page explains how to request deletion of Facebook and Instagram social publishing data connected through ScheduleRama.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main class="legal-wrap">
    <article class="legal-card">
      <div class="legal-meta">
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span>Last Updated</span>
          <strong>August 3, 2026</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <p>This page explains how to request deletion of social publishing data connected to Facebook and Instagram through ScheduleRama.</p>
        <p>These instructions apply to ScheduleRama's <strong>Social Publishing</strong> feature, including connected Facebook Pages, connected Instagram professional accounts, publishing destinations, and related social publishing records.</p>
        <p>For general privacy questions, contact us using the information at the bottom of this page.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2>What This Covers</h2>
        <p>ScheduleRama allows authorized school or organization administrators to connect Facebook and Instagram destinations for publishing school athletics content.</p>
        <p>This page covers deletion of data related to that connection, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Social publishing connection records</li>
          <li>Stored access credentials or tokens used for publishing</li>
          <li>Connected Page and Instagram destination mappings</li>
          <li>Social publishing draft, publish, and delivery records tied to those connections</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout">This page does <strong>not</strong> describe deletion of all school scheduling data or deletion of an entire ScheduleRama organization workspace.</div>

        <h2>How to Request Deletion</h2>
        <p>You may request deletion in either of the following ways.</p>

        <h3>Option 1 — Disconnect inside ScheduleRama</h3>
        <p>If your organization uses ScheduleRama Social Publishing, an authorized administrator can remove the connection from inside the product.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Sign in to ScheduleRama</li>
          <li>Open <strong>Social Publishing</strong></li>
          <li>Open <strong>Connections</strong></li>
          <li>Select the connected Facebook or Instagram connection</li>
          <li>Choose <strong>Disable</strong> or remove the connection</li>
        </ol>
        <p>If a school was assigned to one or more destinations under that connection, those destination assignments will no longer be available for future publishing after the connection is removed.</p>

        <h3>Option 2 — Email us</h3>
        <p>If you want ScheduleRama to delete connected social publishing data, email us at <strong>hello@schedulerama.com</strong> with the subject line <strong>Social Publishing Data Deletion Request</strong>.</p>
        <p>Please include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your full name</li>
          <li>Your school or organization name</li>
          <li>The email address associated with your ScheduleRama access</li>
          <li>The Facebook Page or Instagram account involved, if known</li>
          <li>Whether you want a single social connection removed, all social publishing connections for a school removed, or review of a broader privacy request</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If we need to verify your identity or authority to act for a school or organization, we will contact you before processing the request.</p>

        <h2>What We Delete</h2>
        <p>When a valid deletion request is processed for social publishing data, ScheduleRama will delete or disable, as applicable:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Social publishing access tokens and stored publishing credentials</li>
          <li>Connected Facebook Page identifiers and Instagram destination mappings stored for publishing</li>
          <li>School-to-destination assignment records for the removed connection</li>
          <li>Social publishing draft and publish records that are no longer needed for operational or audit purposes</li>
          <li>Social publishing delivery status records related to the removed connection, subject to any required retention</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If a connection is removed, ScheduleRama will no longer be able to publish new posts to those Facebook or Instagram destinations unless a new connection is created later.</p>

        <h2>What We May Retain</h2>
        <p>ScheduleRama may retain certain limited records where needed for security, fraud prevention, abuse review, system integrity, legal compliance, or internal auditing.</p>
        <p>We may also retain athletics scheduling records that are independent of the Facebook or Instagram connection itself, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>School records</li>
          <li>Team records</li>
          <li>Game and schedule records</li>
          <li>Social post artwork or draft content not required to maintain the removed connection, where retention is necessary for operational records or organization history</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Removing a Facebook or Instagram connection does not automatically delete a school's schedules, teams, or game data from ScheduleRama.</p>

        <h2>Posts Already Published</h2>
        <p>Posts that were already published to Facebook or Instagram are published to the destination account itself. Removing the connection from ScheduleRama does not guarantee removal of posts that were already published on those external platforms.</p>
        <p>If you want previously published posts removed from Facebook or Instagram, remove them directly from the destination account or page using the tools provided by Meta.</p>

        <h2>Timeline</h2>
        <p>ScheduleRama will review deletion requests within a reasonable time after receipt.</p>
        <p>If we need identity or organization authorization verification, the request may take longer. If your request is unusually complex, we may contact you to clarify scope before completion.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p><strong>ScheduleRama</strong><br />
        Privacy: <strong>hello@schedulerama.com</strong><br />
        Support: <strong>hello@schedulerama.com</strong></p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
